@startuml chat_route_walk
' v26 — per-role routing: one turn's walk over the chat route, drawn for the
' two-seat route the Settings UI edits; the mechanism itself takes N seats.
' See docs/design-addendum-provider.md §M.
!include _style.puml
title ChatClient — one turn walks the route (v26)

start
:route = ai::routeFor(Feature::Chat)
<i>read at fire time; a missing route key</i>
<i>DERIVES the v25 provider — no migration write</i>;
:planRoute() — drop seats cooling
in the breaker (unreachable < 20 s ago);
if (any seat left?) then (no)
  #F7E9E8:fail FAST, naming the seats
  "… unreachable — will retry shortly";
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:try **seat #1**
(TICKTIMER_AI_DOWN forces
unreachable before any socket);
if (answered 200 with text?) then (yes)
  #EDF4F1:breaker.noteOk — reply shown;
  stop
else (no)
endif
if (REFUSED? 401 403 404 429 5xx / bad reply) then (yes)
  #F7E9E8:fail LOUDLY — never falls through
  <i>a wrong key masked by a quieter seat costs an</i>
  <i>evening of "why did the answers get dumber"</i>;
  stop
else (no — UNREACHABLE)
endif
:breaker.noteUnreachable(seat #1)
transcript, local-only:
"⚠ <seat 1> unreachable — trying <seat 2>…";
if (a next seat in the route?) then (no)
  #F7E9E8:failed — "couldn't reach the AI service";
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:try **seat #2** — same three verdicts;
if (answered 200 with text?) then (yes)
  #EDF4F1:reply shown **plus attribution**:
  "answered by <seat 2>" — a fallback
  answer names its author;
  stop
else (no)
endif
#F7E9E8:refused -> loud; unreachable -> noted,
and the LAST seat has nowhere to go:
"couldn't reach the AI service";
stop

note right
  §E's one rule, drawn: only the
  UNREACHABLE class (nothing
  answered) moves to the next seat.
  Everything a server actually SAID
  is config feedback the user
  must hear.
end note
@enduml
